// Waybar "custom/kidlock" module for the classroom keyboard lock.
// Tested against the kidlock CLI in this repo. On Omarchy 4+ the default bar
// is Quickshell-based (see ../quickshell/); use this file on systems that
// still run Waybar (older Omarchy, stock Hyprland setups).
//
// INSTALL (Waybar):
//   1. Merge the "custom/kidlock" object below into your waybar config's
//      "modules-center" array, e.g.:
//          "modules-center": ["custom/kidlock", "clock"],
//   2. Append ../waybar/kidlock.css (this repo's waybar/kidlock.css) to your
//      waybar style.css.
//   3. Reload waybar:  pkill waybar; waybar &   (or: systemctl --user restart waybar)
//   4. Click the module with the MOUSE to toggle. Keyboard cannot toggle it
//      while locked -- that is the point.
//
// The module polls `kidlock status --waybar` (JSON, never fails) every
// 2 seconds. Clicking runs `kidlock toggle`. Polling (not signals) is used
// on purpose: the widget recovers on its own if it ever misses an event.

{
  "custom/kidlock": {
    "exec": "kidlock status --waybar",
    "return-type": "json",
    "interval": 2,
    "on-click": "kidlock toggle",
    "on-click-right": "kidlock unlock",
    "tooltip": true,
    "escape": true
  }
}
